<compactness theorem>[Finite satisfiability] means that every finite <subset> $T_0\subseteq T$ has an $L$-structure satisfying all its sentences. Different finite <subsets> may have different witnessing structures. The first-order <compactness theorem> says this condition is equivalent to satisfiability of the entire <set>, but <compactness theorem>[finite satisfiability] itself is defined by the finite-subset condition.

