Satisfiability means that there exists one nonempty-domain $L$-structure $M$ such that $M\models\phi$ for every $\phi\in T$. It is this single simultaneous <first-order model>[model] that is required. By the soundness and completeness theorems, satisfiability is equivalent to syntactic <consistent first-order theory>[consistency] in classical <first-order logic>.

